    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "依也。上曰衣，下曰裳。象覆二人之形。凡衣之屬皆从衣。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Pictogram (象形) Outline of the chest, upper clothing. Compare to the upper part of 文.\nThis pictogram 衣 can be split into two parts and hold another component (e.g., 裹, 衮, 褱, 襄, and 𧝑 as used in 㞡 > 展). See also the top component of 雜.\nTraditionally derived from Proto-Sino-Tibetan *w(y)a-t ~ wit (“to wear; to clothe”), whence Burmese ဝတ် (wat, “to wear”) (Schuessler, 2007), though the Baxter-Sagart reconstruction makes this phonetically suspect.\nPronunciation 2 (\"to wear\") is the exoactive form of pronunciation 1 (\"garment; clothes\") formed with the Old Chinese suffix *-s."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "依也。上曰衣，下曰裳。象覆二人之形。凡衣之屬皆从衣。",
  "shuowenExplanation": "To lean on; to depend. top, clothes, under. Pictograph depicting the form of cover two man. All characters in the 衣 \"clothes\" category use this as radical.",
